    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "PIP",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "Changes in life expectancy in Czechoslovakia since 1920 are examined by sex. The authors note that although life expectancy has increased over time, the trends since 1960 have been less favorable, particularly for men. The major causes of death are described. The authors suggest that further improvements in life expectancy will more likely be achieved through preventive measures rather than curative medicine. (summary in ENG, RUS)"
    }
